 XOP(LONG,  6)
+/*
+ * HOST (18.13, experiment): call a definition that the emulator holds (written
+ * in C) over its own space of variables, not over the space of the program.
+ * One copy to SYS carries the request: the record (arg = the number of the
+ * definition) and right after it, in the same copy, the argument bits (the
+ * payload, as the data of EXEC). The emulator puts the payload at the start
+ * of its own space (the place the definition is set to read: values, or an
+ * image of cells), runs the definition and returns its results by copying:
+ * the image of the result (as many bits as the definition makes) to the
+ * position off[31:0] of the program space, and the 32-bit return value (numeric)
+ * to the position off[63:32]. The positions are given by the call; the emulator
+ * knows nothing of the layout of the data of the caller. The results are in
+ * the program space from the next tick (the same rule as for the answer of
+ * SYS). Answer: status 0, EINVAL (unknown definition, short payload, a result
+ * that does not fit), EFAULT (a result position outside the space). chan, flags: unused.
+ */
+XOP(HOST,  7)
 /* reserve: SPAWN, POLL, MMAP, ... */
 
 XFIELD(req, op,    8)
